


RRESTORE(8C)        UNIX Programmer's Manual         RRESTORE(8C)



NAME
     rrestore - restore a file system dump across the network

SYNOPSIS
     /etc/rrestore [ key [ name ... ]

DESCRIPTION
     _R_r_e_s_t_o_r_e obtains from magnetic tape files saved by a previ-
     ous _d_u_m_p(8).  The command is identical in operation to
     _r_e_s_t_o_r_e(8) except the _f key should be specified and the file
     supplied should be of the form _m_a_c_h_i_n_e:_d_e_v_i_c_e.

     _R_r_e_s_t_o_r_e creates a remote server, /_e_t_c/_r_m_t, on the client
     machine to access the tape device.

SEE ALSO
     restore(8), rmt(8C)

DIAGNOSTICS
     Same as _r_e_s_t_o_r_e(8) with a few extra related to the network.



































